# Liveness use-after-move: a mover of the WHOLE place at arg 0 followed by a read
# of a SUB-place under it (`f(!n, n.data)`). Under the ratified pass-order rider
# (liveness precedes aliasing), the `!n` move at arg 0 dominates the later read
# of `n.data` (left-to-right eval), so this is E_UseAfterMove — the self-host
# emits `use of `n` after it was moved`, NOT the place-overlap diagnostic. This
# matches production/ggdef (ggdef's single `Slot::Moved`→IllFormed); the
# self-host emits a SINGLE UAM here, one cleaner than production's redundant
# UAM+BorrowConflict double-fire (a filed LOW Rust-gg wart).
struct N:
    Vector[int] data

void f(N !a, Vector[int] b):
    pass

void run():
    N n = N(Vector[int]())
    f(!n, n.data)

void main():
    run()
